Subject : GEFCO Meeting Minutes


To: CCM, CCE, WCG, ASG, WSM, ASM, European offices
Cc: LEHBB
Fm: UCM

Dear all,

Please find minutes of meeting held at GEFCO H/O in Paris

Setting
GEFCO H/O, Paris, October 29th 2013
Participants:

  *   Gefco: Johannes Nanninga, Head of Procurement (Air and Sea)
  *   Gefco: Philippe Maupin, Ocean Freight Procurement
  *   HJS: LEHBBG, BBS, BBS/Didier Jean, UCM



Main Discussion topics

  *   Introduction of new LEHBBG, BBS
  *   Gefco overview:
     *   25% owned by PSA (Peugeot Citroen), 75% by Russian Railways (Previously 100% subsidiary of Peugeot)
     *   Specialized in Automotive Logistics as per previous ownership, they are now heavily diversifying their cargo mixture
     *   5 business units: Trucking, finished vehicules logistics, Customs/Tax declarations, Wharehousing, Air & Sea Freight
     *   Main expansion markets to be: Latam, Asia, East Europe (incl. Russia). Weak position in SEA, US, India
     *   Developing a block train product from China to Eastern Europe
     *   Currently handling 120,000 TEUs for Ocean
        *   Latam = 35% of TTL handling vol. mostly out of LEH
        *   AESW/AESE match back ratio = 100%
     *   Carrier program: 70% of handle volumes allocated to 10 carriers



Current Business relation status:

  *   HJS = top carrier on AESW for GEFCO
  *   Strong relations in France, GEFCO needs to bring the partnership to a more global level as per their growth plans and needs a more global approach with more local contacts
  *   Procurement to be centralized in Paris and via LEHBB



Next steps



  *   As per customer diversification strategy for 2014, it is necessary that each office and region must develop closer ties with the GEFCO local stations. Please find attached the list of Gefco network




Kind Regards,

UCM


